---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Doctrine" currentPath="/doctrine">

  <span class="meta">II · Doctrine</span>
  <h1 class="doctrine-title">Principles and boundaries</h1>

  <div class="page-content">

    <section class="doctrine-intro">
      <h2 class="doctrine-section-title">Purpose</h2>
      <p>House of Laline creates resolved digital structures through clear hierarchy, deliberate pacing and declared boundaries. Each edition may take a different form; its internal logic remains stable.</p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2 class="doctrine-section-title">Structural logic</h2>

      <h3>Pacing</h3>
      <p>Content unfolds in predictable intervals, never accelerating to create urgency or stalling to create drama. Each page operates at the same cognitive speed. Users traverse depth, not breadth.</p>

      <h3>Hierarchy</h3>
      <p>Authority emerges from vertical clarity. Primary navigation is sparse. Secondary navigation remains visibly subordinate and appears only where it belongs. Tertiary layers never compete with their parent structure. Depth is communicated through consistent indentation and containment, not visual flourish.</p>

      <h3>Repetition</h3>
      <p>Within an edition, repeated page types retain the same hierarchy, spacing and behaviour. Across editions, composition may change because purpose changes. Repetition is not a universal visual style; it is the cognitive infrastructure that allows each system to be learned once.</p>

      <h3>Interaction density</h3>
      <p>Interactions are rationed. Interactivity is deployed only when it prevents fragmentation. Everything else is static traversal: click, load, read. No hover states that reveal critical information. No progressive disclosure that hides structural relationships. Density is achieved through layering pages, not layering interface.</p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2 class="doctrine-section-title">Fixed system</h2>

      <h3>Page types</h3>
      <dl class="definition-list doctrine-definition-list">
        <dt>Index</dt>
        <dd>Maps a complete set of routes, categories or records within a declared boundary.</dd>

        <dt>Collection</dt>
        <dd>Presents a complete inventory within a defined boundary, with its metadata and scope made explicit.</dd>

        <dt>Document</dt>
        <dd>Houses singular content in a stable reading order with a restrained internal hierarchy.</dd>

        <dt>Entry point</dt>
        <dd>Establishes identity and purpose, then provides a clear route into the edition or collection.</dd>
      </dl>

      <div class="edition-boundaries" aria-label="Edition boundaries">
        <div>
          <h3>Fixed within an edition</h3>
          <p>Navigation relationships, typographic hierarchy, spacing logic, page behaviours and declared content boundaries.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Replaceable within an edition</h3>
          <p>Content in declared fields, new records following the established type, archive dates and version information.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Variable across editions</h3>
          <p>Grid, palette, tempo, page types, image behaviour and interaction when the purpose of the work requires them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2 class="doctrine-section-title">Explicit constraints</h2>

      <div class="constraint-groups">
        <div class="constraint-group">
          <h3>Must never exist</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Promotional language that invents urgency or scarcity</li>
            <li>Essential content concealed behind transient interaction</li>
            <li>Navigation that changes through inferred user behaviour</li>
            <li>Essential media without an equivalent description or attribution</li>
            <li>Content designed to expire or become inaccessible</li>
            <li>Social proof, testimonials or persuasive framing</li>
            <li>Analytics-driven interface adaptation</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="constraint-group">
          <h3>Allowed only sparingly</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Diagrams, when prose cannot represent the relationship clearly</li>
            <li>Tables, when fixed attributes require systematic comparison</li>
            <li>Accordions, when they prevent one concept being fragmented across pages</li>
            <li>Search, when manual browsing no longer provides reasonable access</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="constraint-group">
          <h3>Must remain predictable</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Page and route behaviour</li>
            <li>Link appearance and destination</li>
            <li>Heading hierarchy and reading order</li>
            <li>Error states and paths to resolution</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2 class="doctrine-section-title">Role of interactivity</h2>

      <h3>When it adds authority</h3>
      <p>Interactivity adds authority when it preserves context that would otherwise fragment. Expandable sections keep related information on a single page. Anchor links allow direct citation without creating orphaned content. Sortable tables reveal different organizational logic without duplicating data. In these cases, the interaction is structural; it changes how information is viewed without altering what information is available.</p>

      <h3>When it weakens clarity</h3>
      <p>Interactivity weakens clarity when it conceals structure, creates ambiguity about state, introduces temporal dependencies, or substitutes performance for clarity. Any interaction that makes the user question 'what is here?' or 'where am I?' is disqualifying.</p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2 class="doctrine-section-title">Rejection list</h2>
      <ul class="rejection-list">
        <li>Decorative hero sections without structural purpose</li>
        <li>Conversion-led calls to action</li>
        <li>Personalization engines</li>
        <li>Infinite scroll</li>
        <li>Modal overlays</li>
        <li>Feature comparison matrices</li>
        <li>Related content algorithms</li>
        <li>Newsletter signup forms</li>
        <li>Any language suggesting urgency, scarcity, or timeliness</li>
        <li>Vanity metrics</li>
        <li>A/B testing of structure or navigation</li>
        <li>Dark patterns of any kind</li>
        <li>Core reading that requires JavaScript to become available</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer class="page-signature">
      - House of Laline
    </footer>

  </div>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doctrine-title {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem !important;
    font-family: var(--font-display) !important;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 2.6vw, 2.25rem) !important;
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium) !important;
    line-height: 1.1 !important;
    letter-spacing: 0 !important;
    text-transform: none !important;
  }

  .page-content {
    max-width: var(--content-max);
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
  }

  .page-content hr {
    margin: 2.75rem 0 !important;
  }

  .doctrine-section-title {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem !important;
    font-family: var(--font-display) !important;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.4vw, 1.9rem) !important;
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium) !important;
    line-height: 1.15 !important;
    letter-spacing: 0 !important;
    text-transform: none !important;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.65rem !important;
    font-family: var(--font-display) !important;
    font-size: 1.2rem !important;
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium) !important;
    font-style: normal !important;
    line-height: 1.25 !important;
    letter-spacing: 0 !important;
    text-transform: none !important;
    color: var(--color-identity-ink) !important;
  }

  .doctrine-intro p { max-width: 42rem; }

  /* Page types */
  .doctrine-definition-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(7rem, 0.35fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    margin: 0 !important;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .doctrine-definition-list dt,
  .doctrine-definition-list dd {
    margin: 0 !important;
    padding: 1rem 0 !important;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .doctrine-definition-list dt {
    padding-right: 1.5rem !important;
    font-family: var(--font-display) !important;
    font-size: 1.1rem !important;
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium) !important;
    line-height: 1.35 !important;
    letter-spacing: 0 !important;
    text-transform: none !important;
    color: var(--color-identity-ink) !important;
  }

  .doctrine-definition-list dd {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    font-weight: var(--weight-light);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-reading-ink);
  }

  /* What an edition holds fixed */
  .edition-boundaries {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .edition-boundaries > div,
  .constraint-group {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 0.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .edition-boundaries h3,
  .constraint-group h3 {
    margin: 0 !important;
  }

  .edition-boundaries p {
    margin: 0 !important;
    line-height: 1.65 !important;
  }

  /* Lists */
  ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-sm) 0 var(--space-md);
  }

  ul li {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    font-weight: var(--weight-light);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    padding: 0.35rem 0;
    padding-left: 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    position: relative;
  }

  ul li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .constraint-groups {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .constraint-group ul {
    margin: 0 !important;
  }

  .constraint-group li {
    padding: 0 0 0.45rem !important;
    border-bottom: 0;
    line-height: 1.6 !important;
  }

  .constraint-group li:last-child { padding-bottom: 0 !important; }

  .rejection-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: 2rem;
    margin: 0 !important;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .rejection-list li {
    padding: 0.65rem 0 !important;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    line-height: 1.5 !important;
  }

  :global(.main--content) .page-signature {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-family: var(--font-display) !important;
    font-size: 1rem !important;
    font-style: italic !important;
    font-weight: var(--weight-regular) !important;
    line-height: var(--leading-body) !important;
    letter-spacing: 0 !important;
    text-transform: none !important;
    color: var(--color-identity-ink) !important;
    transform: translateY(1.25rem);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .doctrine-definition-list,
    .edition-boundaries > div,
    .constraint-group,
    .rejection-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .doctrine-definition-list dt {
      padding-bottom: 0.25rem !important;
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .doctrine-definition-list dd { padding-top: 0 !important; }

    .edition-boundaries > div,
    .constraint-group { gap: 0.75rem; }
  }
</style>
